789
00:59:34,120 --> 00:59:41,800
Rym: And I think the main thing it's got going for it is it's... Not only is it great characters, great animation, great voice acting, a pretty compelling story.

790
00:59:42,201 --> 00:59:55,080
Rym: It's short, but it looks like... You know the thing we always complain about where there's concept art that looks great, but then when the thing comes out, it's a much more distilled, refined version?

791
00:59:55,660 --> 00:59:57,747
Rym: This looks like concept art.

792
00:59:57,967 --> 01:00:01,077
Rym: The show is animated like concept art.

793
01:00:01,238 --> 01:00:01,920
Rym: It's beautiful.

794
01:00:04,802 --> 01:00:07,090
Rym: I think it is literally one of the best animated things I've seen.

795
01:00:07,110 --> 01:00:09,599
Rym: that was not the Spider-Verse in many years.

796
01:00:11,730 --> 01:00:12,119
Rym: Top five.

797
01:00:13,880 --> 01:00:16,644
Rym: What I would not watch is any more Dragon Prince.

798
01:00:16,904 --> 01:00:19,367
Rym: We tried to watch the next new season.

799
01:00:19,387 --> 01:00:21,971
Rym: No, the show is not good.

800
01:00:23,152 --> 01:00:26,456
Rym: What we saw back in the day is... Just pretend that's all there is.

801
01:00:26,517 --> 01:00:29,200
Rym: It is not worth continuing, unfortunately.

802
01:00:33,425 --> 01:00:34,170
Rym: All right, BNA.

803
01:00:34,190 --> 01:00:35,720
Rym: So I've got to watch Cyberpunk.

804
01:00:37,577 --> 01:00:37,640
Scott: Eh.

805
01:00:39,021 --> 01:00:42,150
Rym: All the anime people I know have said that Cyberpunk is phenomenal.

806
01:00:43,433 --> 01:00:45,259
Rym: If you want to see some Spriggan-style...

807
01:00:45,901 --> 01:00:48,460
Scott: Ooh, the Sting is on Netflix, but I've seen that.

808
01:00:48,580 --> 01:00:49,062
Rym: I've seen that.

809
01:00:49,363 --> 01:00:54,340
Rym: We actually randomly, on New Year's Eve, we watched It's a Wonderful Life just because we both hadn't seen it recently.

810
01:00:54,661 --> 01:00:55,299
Scott: It's a good movie.

811
01:00:56,141 --> 01:00:56,282
Rym: Yeah.

812
01:00:56,542 --> 01:01:02,179
Rym: Because I remembered what you'd said because you'd watched it again not that long ago and I think you said...

813
01:01:02,501 --> 01:01:04,000
Scott: It's just real white, but you know.

814
01:01:04,000 --> 01:01:06,043
Rym: Yep, it is real white.

815
01:01:06,143 --> 01:01:17,060
Rym: We also noted that, but I feel like most people saw that movie as a kid or only actually ever saw a few specific scenes from it and have a perception of what it's about.

816
01:01:17,360 --> 01:01:19,020
Rym: But really, it's mostly anti-capitalist.

817
01:01:19,620 --> 01:01:21,124
Scott: That's exactly what it is, yes.

818
01:01:21,927 --> 01:01:24,374
Scott: Just like Christmas Carol.

819
01:01:24,795 --> 01:01:26,440
Scott: Most Christmas shit is anti-capitalist.

820
01:01:31,850 --> 01:01:34,220
Rym: This has been GeekNights with Rym and Scott.

821
01:01:34,280 --> 01:01:36,790
Rym: Special thanks to DJ Pretzel for the opening theme.

822
01:01:36,970 --> 01:01:43,010
Scott: Be sure to visit our website at frontrowclue.com for show notes, discussion, links and more.

823
01:01:43,510 --> 01:01:46,182
Rym: Remember, GeekNights is not one but four different shows.

824
01:01:46,483 --> 01:01:48,050
Rym: Mondays are science and technology.

825
01:01:48,190 --> 01:01:49,935
Rym: Tuesdays, gaming and games.

826
01:01:50,056 --> 01:01:51,861
Rym: Wednesdays are animation and comics.

827
01:01:52,182 --> 01:01:54,670
Rym: Thursdays are arbitrary and indiscriminate.

828
01:01:55,350 --> 01:02:00,230
Rym: GeekNights is distributed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License.

829
01:02:00,691 --> 01:02:05,041
Scott: GeekNights is recorded live with no studio and no audience.

830
01:02:05,522 --> 01:02:08,970
Scott: But unlike those other late shows, it's actually recorded at night.

831
01:02:09,351 --> 01:02:24,410
Rym: And the Patreon patrons for this episode of GeekNights are... Alan Joyce, Linky G. Dredd, Lily Tenenbaum, Kace Karr, Max Music, Chris Haddad, Christopher Orr, Clinton, Walton, Finn, Joel Hayes, Betty Rymer, Rebecca Dunn, Sam Erickson, Trevor Von Hurl, and a bunch of people who do not want me to say their names.

832
01:02:25,130 --> 01:02:36,921
Rym: So the things I've been reading that are not fiction, that Scott would make fun of me for lately, and I am not kidding, are the various NATO standardization documents.

833
01:02:37,402 --> 01:02:40,370
Rym: And I have both a personal and a professional interest in these.

834
01:02:40,971 --> 01:02:43,678
Rym: But that's the story for another time.

835
01:02:44,079 --> 01:02:48,210
Rym: Tonight, I leave you with some music from a cartoon I made.

